abstract: >-
  ADHTEB (Alzheimer’s Disease Harmonization Text Embedding
  Benchmark) is a Python package designed to evaluate the
  performance of text-embedding models in harmonizing
  variable descriptions from diverse cohorts in the context
  of Alzheimer’s disease.


  As general purpose benchmarks often lack domain-specific
  evaluation for clinical data, this benchmark is
  specifically designed to evaluate the performance of
  embedding models for harmonization or clustering of data
  descriptins in a clinical setting.
